    "narrative": "The primary focus for LawDog today centers on the elite scoring output of **Lawrence Butler** (71.26), **Bryson Stott** (71.23), and **Taylor Ward** (71.19). **Lawrence Butler** holds the highest efficiency rating on the board, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against P\u00e9rez and a clean middle-of-the-order opportunity that maximizes his run production potential. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** and **Taylor Ward** are clear-cut starters due to massive SP skill advantages; **Bryson Stott** faces a struggling Avila, and while he faces a slight penalty for the catcher's elite hold rate, his volume in the 5x5 categories remains too high to bench. **Taylor Ward** thrives in his platoon advantage against Lodolo, with the favorable park factors bolstering a strong base projection that solidifies his role as a cornerstone of today\u2019s lineup.\n\nStrategic decisions in the outfield and middle infield emphasize the scarcity of stolen bases. **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.69) is prioritized over **Daulton Varsho** (52.12) due to a superior matchup against Gordon, where the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher provides a critical green light for the base paths. **Geraldo Perdomo** (59.18) occupies the UTIL spot, narrowly edging out **Gavin Sheets** (48.63). **Gavin Sheets** was the most difficult exclusion; despite a decent projection, the lingering uncertainty of his lineup spot\u2014officially listed as \"Lineup Pending\"\u2014rendered him a riskier play compared to the confirmed floor of **Geraldo Perdomo**. \n\nWe continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving a significant void in our power-speed production that we are currently compensating for with the collective volume of **Jonathan Aranda** and **Masyn Winn**. While **Cal Raleigh** (63.15) faces a tough matchup against Yesavage, his role in the #3 spot ensures we aren't sacrificing valuable run-scoring opportunities despite the SP skill headwind. Managers should note that **Luis Arraez** (65.15) remains a high-floor play, relying on his elite batting average profile and a +14% park boost to offset the presence of Gordon on the mound.",
